===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|sadelen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sadolian}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sadulōną}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|saddl}}

# To put a saddle on an animal.
# To get into a saddle.
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[burden]] or [[encumber]].
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To give a [[responsibility]] to someone.
#: ''He has been '''saddled''' with the task of collecting evidence to the theft.''

